# Per-user containment for the shared devvm (setup-devvm.sh §10, 2026-06-22;
# MemoryHigh dropped 2026-07-02; swap bounded rather than off 2026-09-02).
# Applies to EACH user-<uid>.slice = all of one user's ssh/tmux work. Mirrors
# the t3-serve@.service caps so a user is bounded in whichever surface they
# work in.
#
# MemorySwapMax was 0 from 2026-06-22, because a user runaway had
# swap-thrashed the throttled virtual disk into an I/O storm and the box was
# hard-killed. It is now a CEILING instead of a ban, for a reason the earlier
# setting could not accommodate: a session's memory is otherwise entirely
# unswappable, so the kernel's only move at the cap is to kill the
# conversation, and pages from the RAM-backed /tmp charged to a pane cannot be
# paged out at all. A bound keeps the original lesson — the 2026-06-22 storm
# ran swap to 15 GB, and no single user can now approach that — while giving
# the kernel somewhere to put a session instead of killing it.
#
# MemoryHigh stays infinity even now. A hog plateauing in a high..max band
# livelocks the entire slice (every ssh/tmux session of that user) instead of
# dying, and a 4G swap ceiling does not change that: past the ceiling the band
# is unreclaimable again. Straight-to-OOM at MemoryMax remains the containment
# (see post-mortem addendum 2026-07-02).
# MemoryLow is the fairness knob, added 2026-09-12. It is a protected floor:
# reclaim leaves a slice's pages alone up to this size and takes from whoever is
# above theirs instead. That is what "equal share under contention" means for
# memory, which has no weight the way CPU and IO do.
#
# It is work-conserving with no extra machinery. An empty slice protects
# nothing, so one user alone still gets most of the box and is only reclaimed
# when somebody else actually needs the memory. Absent users therefore cost
# zero, which is why this stays a uniform value on the user-.slice template
# rather than per-uid drop-ins: anca and breakglass are covered automatically
# if they ever return, and reserve nothing while they are away.
#
# Sized for the active population rather than the enrolled one. Protection is
# best-effort, so it stops meaning anything once every remaining page sits
# inside somebody's floor and reclaim proceeds regardless. On 31 GiB with two
# active humans, 8.5 GiB each plus 2 GiB for system.slice leaves roughly 12 GiB
# unprotected, which is the headroom that makes the floors real.
#
# Why this was needed: measured 2026-09-12, wizard's slice had re-read 609 GiB
# of file pages against 196 MiB of anonymous pages since boot, a ratio of 3183
# to 1. With MemorySwapMax reached, reclaim cannot page anon out, so it evicts
# file cache and the box re-reads it from a spindle. Floors make that eviction
# land on whoever is over their share instead of on an idle user's session.
[Slice]
MemoryAccounting=yes
MemoryLow={{ devvm_user_memory_low }}
MemoryHigh=infinity
MemoryMax={{ devvm_user_memory_max }}
MemorySwapMax={{ devvm_user_swap_max }}
CPUAccounting=yes
CPUWeight=100
IOAccounting=yes
IOWeight=100
